  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_0124d99d785e445c8888c6294c946b3b",
      "statement": "The repository's standard checks are `pytest` and `ruff check .`; the multi-process CPU gloo harness `tests/ddp.py::run_ddp_two_rank` (spawning workers that each write a per-rank result JSON) is the shared seam for every distributed test, and the focused distributed tests must be re-run after changing rank gates, sampler assumptions, reduction code, validation callbacks, trainer device selection, or checkpoint monitors.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://pyproject.toml#L96-L101",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5aae0962ef04ad9c0c1982bc1a9ffeb1b7a64be2f18f2ca1a6a34c2360315bf3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/ddp.py#L71-L94",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:59017ed3023831e2fadd4f71478ac6d9cd61837565af8bf76f342c00b8bcad58:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_58047773030c4143a3096c463d771731",
      "statement": "The in-training paired-fidelity observer is shipped and default-on for `manifold-train-controlnet`: `run_controlnet_training` registers the `paired_fidelity` spec and passes `default_names=[\"train_loss\", \"checkpoint\", \"paired_fidelity\"]`, and the observer stays observe-only — never a checkpoint `monitor_metric` (selection stays `val/x0_mae`), never a loss term, and never touching the optimizer or EMA.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired_callback.py#L1-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4a18ef56a296f7054c2e16f65485deaf58032217aa270a95fc8eaa82b304e402:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/paired_fidelity.py#L36-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2c220edce50b7369395e72c29eca98fc1baeff8a1c5ed61188da0f3ef97a12a3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/controlnet_cli.py#L168-L198",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5446a4872d3a7c262ac18f17012b78d5d9325c828070feb27d14d31fdce070bd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f65bc9139aaa43e69693d374dd5d40b9",
      "statement": "The paired-fidelity observer's DDP design is redundant evaluation rather than sharding: every rank scores the same fixed subset under identical seeded noise on DDP-synchronized weights, so the per-rank values are identical and Lightning's torchmetrics sync is the only cross-rank interaction — there is no FID-style sharding and no error-rendezvous machinery.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired_callback.py#L22-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:53e5296f948ef16052ab4a8dbcd5b65c117dc575d3f849d542bd7308aaf1d387:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_paired_fidelity_ddp.py#L19-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bb1a558ae1294084763ac1a15733c0dc9035300d5a32efe9a6fbb4cd3506d73c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e9a59dcff090483c9675d6b0d799a6fb",
      "statement": "The paired-fidelity observer resolves its paired validation dataset lazily at the first gated epoch (the cold path replaces `val_latent_ds` during `DataModule.setup()`), caches a seeded `randperm` subset so only the model changes between epochs, and re-seeds the generation noise from a fresh generator on every gated epoch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired_callback.py#L125-L146",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3175cd9f3cec4eb18fe33df9a6911bba48dd61d1cccc699a006b8f023224ee8b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired_callback.py#L179-L196",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:59d251d2fab59a14facd6366e78b72bd5b3d22d2092d769c0b2d981ced1dee4f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_929ffc1fe8fa405895c8fa5f1666b27d",
      "statement": "Under DDP, `val/x0_mae` reduces to the true sample-weighted global mean: `LatentX0MAE` attaches a `torchmetrics.MeanMetric` to the module and updates it with the per-batch sample count as the weight, so Lightning's cross-rank sync yields `(Σ mae·B)/(Σ B)` rather than a mean of per-rank means.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/metrics.py#L109-L147",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5fa212124743be6153006f80ac7f909e2bf388a581efc71adef42e519a89d88d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b09666a5d1524126994bf152f2b962a7",
      "statement": "Distributed FID reduces per-plane sufficient statistics `(sum_x, sum_xxT, n)` to global moments instead of gathering feature matrices: an empty local shard contributes correctly sized zero statistics, the synthetic arm is rank-strided (`seed + global_index`) so the global sample union matches the requested count, and a plane is valid only once the global count reaches two.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/fid/reducer.py#L16-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bf6c58d9af909b4f254eccc177926a226722952437846e88f4efd8ac6aca8240:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/fid/rollout.py#L60-L77",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:34e7e9e60cebe66b0699dfd6309bcceff035cac6ace3fb502e862d27314edac0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_daec3bad0ed548a28d8d4fe293ec8bd5",
      "statement": "The FID callback preserves collective-count invariance with four symmetric error-rendezvous all-reduces (stage error, feature-net disablement, real-plane preprocessing error, synthetic-plane preprocessing error), so a rank-local failure cannot strand peers in a later reduction; a failed rendezvous logs `val/fid` as `inf` on every rank.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/fid/callback.py#L215-L386",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1e4e4650b702ab4868ee3927c47f157aa9d149c5e818a51b62053ab71a4cabe5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f7d9855994bb4ff2a4318a6bcd2fb820",
      "statement": "`val/mean_reward` is a manually reduced global value: every rank accumulates a non-padding `(sum, count)` pair over its own validation shard, the pair is `all_reduce`d (SUM) at epoch end, and the global mean is logged with `sync_dist=False` — a manually `all_reduce`d value must not also use `sync_dist=True` for the same value.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/grpo.py#L521-L534",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5ee52fb9f5d0e9cf9d883507e5c24c1ffe3f74a10ff4a1c8ce327083a9a73742:"
        },
